# Online / Offline — two overlapping avatar stacks (4 online, 3 offline) in pill backgrounds; every tap anywhere moves a random avatar to the other group: it springs across (LinearTransition), its grayscale filter animates, and both pills resize (pills fade in/out when a group empties).
# What this test covers: single taps with each transition fully settled, taps while the layout springs are still
# running, a long burst that is likely to empty one group (the forced-direction branch, pill exiting/entering with
# FadeOut/FadeIn), taps on and off the avatars (the whole screen is the pressable), and a long press.
# Visual note: on a fresh open only the first online avatar is painted; the others stay blank until they move.
context platform=ios
open "demos://animations/online-offline"
wait "label=\"Close\"" 40000
wait 3000
# Settled single moves.
press 201 437
wait 1200
press 201 437
wait 1200
press 201 600
wait 1200
# Taps while the springs run.
press 201 437
wait 250
press 201 437
wait 250
press 100 300
wait 1500
# Long burst: one of the groups is likely to empty and come back.
press 201 650 --count 14 --interval-ms 120
wait 2000
press 201 650 --count 14 --interval-ms 300
wait 2000
# Long press still triggers onPress on release.
longpress 300 437 900
wait 1500
wait "label=\"Close\"" 10000
press "label=\"Close\""
wait 1500
